# Foreign tickets — stop and confirm

This repo is **`eten-tech-foundation/fluent-mobile`**. Tracker is **org Project 4, view 9 (Fluent Mobile Board)** only. **Not Linear.**

Applies to **Cursor and Claude Code** (and any agent reading these rules via `CLAUDE.md`).

## In scope (no extra confirm)

GitHub issues in **`eten-tech-foundation/fluent-mobile`** that are (or will be) on Project 4. Board edits still follow [project-board.mdc](./project-board.mdc) and [docs/guides/project-board.md](../../docs/guides/project-board.md).

## Out of scope — stop. Do not act.

Treat as foreign until the user **pauses this turn and explicitly confirms**, including:

- Issues in **any other GitHub repo** (other Fluent, ETF, Gloo, or personal repos)
- **Any org/user project that is not Project 4** (including Project 7)
- **Linear** (or Jira, Notion, etc.) tickets
- Status, Priority, assignee, labels, comments, close, or project-item moves on a ticket that is **not** a fluent-mobile issue

Do **not** “helpfully” update, move, or comment on foreign tickets while working here.

## Confirm bar (all must be true)

Vague asks do **not** count: “clean up the board”, “sync tickets”, “while you’re in Linear”, “update the other Fluent tickets”, umbrella/org playbooks, or a blanket “yes”.

1. **Stop.** Do not call GitHub/Linear/project write tools yet.
2. List each ticket: tracker, **repo or project**, ID, and the **exact** mutation.
3. Wait for the user, in **this** conversation, to **name those IDs** and approve **those** mutations.

If confirmation is missing, partial, or ambiguous: **do nothing**. Ask once; do not proceed.